Z||000000||maryjane||06-06-2001||02:12 AM||||I am going to be replacing the right rear qtr<BR>pnl on our 84 se this weekend-I did a search and one of your old posts was the only one that came up. Can you give me some insight before I just blindly "go where I've never gone before"? Or anyone else that has done this? Mostly interested in removing it.Hopefully I can reverse the procedure to install he new one. You can Email me at janedon1@earthlink.net if it is going to be a verylong post.Thanks<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||06-06-2001||09:41 AM||||MaryJane:<P>Paul McKibben has excellent instructions on his web site on removal of the notchback quarter windows.  Check it out at <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A> <P>He also makes very high quality replacement inserts for the quarter windows.  Plus he is a good guy!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||06-06-2001||09:14 PM||||It is the lower passenger side rear qtr panel I'm working on. Sits between the door and rear wheel well. Anybody? 84 SE Thanks,<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||06-06-2001||09:28 PM||||On my '85 SE (as I recall):<P>Remove black rocker panel -- cut or punch plastic rivets, drill-out aluminum rivets in door sills, and remove screws from fender wells<P>Remove quarter trim molding (probably break clips)<P>Remove quarter panel -- drill-out 1/4" aluminum rivets, and cut or punch plastic rivet<P>When I replaced the panel, I got rivets from GM and borrowed a big rivet tool from a mechanic buddy.  You can replace the rocker panel edge rivets with black nylon license plate bolts, and the door sill rivets with Rivet-tite plastic push rivets.  Trim fasteners are available from Fiero Store.<P>Good Luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||06-06-2001||09:48 PM||||Thanks, I've got a big rivet gun at work and plenty of rivets. Guess I better check into trim clips before I start.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||06-06-2001||10:16 PM||||Sorry guys, I guess I didn't read the original post too well!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
